message: >-
  If you use ActionScope in research, please cite the software using the
  metadata in this file.
title: "ActionScope: Coverage-aware analysis of GitHub Actions and AWS IAM evidence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Rishabh
    alias: r12habh
repository-code: "https://github.com/r12habh/ActionScope"
url: "https://r12habh.github.io/ActionScope/"
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
date-released: 2026-08-10
keywords:
  - AWS IAM
  - CI/CD security
  - GitHub Actions
  - OIDC
  - static analysis
  - supply-chain security
abstract: >-
  ActionScope is an open-source Python CLI and GitHub Action that connects
  GitHub Actions credential paths with available AWS IAM evidence. It reports
  recoverable cloud permissions, preserves evidence gaps, and detects
  workflow-layer security exposures such as compromised or mutable actions,
  unsafe token permissions, script injection, and OIDC trust-policy issues.
